IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb3-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), PART XI -- Insider Trading (ss 126 to 131).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Rules are named `<what> within s N`. Part XI defines "insider" twice
-- (s 126(1), "except in section 131", and s 131(1), "in this section"), and "officer" and "share" for
-- itself; each has its own rule and the names carry the section. A "prescribed" percentage, person or
-- circumstance, and a "take-over bid as defined in the regulations", are plain inputs: the regulations
-- are not among the sources. Whether a person is an insider is a plain BOOLEAN input to the offence
-- and liability rules; the rules that work it out are here, and the seat layer joins them.
-- Dates: Part XI holds no enactment, assent or commencement provision, so no date is carried.

§ `Part XI -- Insider Trading`

§§ `s 126(1) -- definitions for this Part`

-- "business combination": three alternatives. Whether a particular acquisition is of "all or
-- substantially all" the property is a judgment of fact, taken as the input.
-- src:1553 | business combination means an acquisition of all or substantially all the property of one body corporate by another, or an amalgamation of two or more bodies corporate, or any similar reorganization between or among two or more bodies corporate; (regroupement d’entreprises)
@ref CBCA s 126(1) business combination (src:1553)
GIVEN `the transaction is an acquisition of all or substantially all the property of one body corporate by another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is an amalgamation of two or more bodies corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is a similar reorganization between or among two or more bodies corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`business combination within s 126(1)` MEANS
        `the transaction is an acquisition of all or substantially all the property of one body corporate by another`
    OR  `the transaction is an amalgamation of two or more bodies corporate`
    OR  `the transaction is a similar reorganization between or among two or more bodies corporate`

-- "insider", for this Part except section 131 (which has its own definition, s 131(1)): four kinds of
-- person. "Distributing corporation" is the s 2(1) term (the keel's `distributing corporation within s 2(1)`;
-- here a plain fact about the corporation). A person may be an insider of the distributing corporation
-- on more than one limb; one is enough.
-- Not an insider by this section: a person who is only an insider in the sense of s 131; ask s 131(1).
-- src:1555 | insider means, except in section 131,
-- src:1556 | (a) a director or officer of a distributing corporation;
-- src:1557 | (b) a director or officer of a subsidiary of a distributing corporation;
-- src:1558 | (c) a director or officer of a body corporate that enters into a business combination with a distributing corporation; and
-- src:1559 | (d) a person employed or retained by a distributing corporation; (initié)
@ref CBCA s 126(1) insider (src:1555-1559)
GIVEN `the term is used in section 131` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director or officer of a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director or officer of a subsidiary of a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director or officer of a body corporate that enters into a business combination with a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed or retained by a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`insider within s 126(1)` MEANS
        (NOT `the term is used in section 131`)
    AND (    `the person is a director or officer of a distributing corporation`
         OR  `the person is a director or officer of a subsidiary of a distributing corporation`
         OR  `the person is a director or officer of a body corporate that enters into a business combination with a distributing corporation`
         OR  `the person is employed or retained by a distributing corporation`)

-- "officer" for this Part. The list is the s 2(1) list WITHOUT its first limb: s 126(1) has no
-- "individual appointed as an officer under section 121". The offices are those "of an entity" (the s 2(1)
-- term, worked out by the keel's `entity within s 2(1)`), and the last limb needs an individual. An
-- officer appointed under s 121 who holds none of the offices and performs no similar function is an
-- officer under s 2(1) but not under this definition (finding 1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:1560 | officer means the chairperson of the board of directors, the president, a vice-president, the secretary, the treasurer, the comptroller, the general counsel, the general manager, a managing director, of an entity, or any other individual who performs functions for an entity similar to those normally performed by an individual occupying any of those offices; (dirigeant)
@ref CBCA s 126(1) officer (src:1560)
GIVEN `the office or function` IS AN Office
      `the holder is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of body the office is in` IS A `Kind of person or entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`officer within s 126(1)` MEANS
        `entity within s 2(1)` `the kind of body the office is in`
    AND CONSIDER `the office or function`
        WHEN `the chairperson of the board of directors` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the president` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a vice-president` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the secretary` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the treasurer` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the comptroller` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the general counsel` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the general manager` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a managing director` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `another individual performing functions similar to those of one of these offices` THEN `the holder is an individual`
        WHEN `an officer appointed under section 121` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `holds no office and performs no similar function` THEN FALSE

-- "share" for this Part: a share carrying voting rights, always or because of an event that has
-- occurred and is continuing; and, included, a security currently convertible into such a share and a
-- currently exercisable option or right to acquire such a share or such a convertible security.
-- src:1561 | share means a share carrying voting rights under all circumstances or by reason of the occurrence of an event that has occurred and that is continuing, and includes
-- src:1562 | (a) a security currently convertible into such a share, and
-- src:1563 | (b) currently exercisable options and rights to acquire such a share or such a convertible security. (action)
@ref CBCA s 126(1) share (src:1561-1563)
GIVEN `it is a share carrying voting rights under all circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a share carrying voting rights by reason of the occurrence of an event that has occurred and that is continuing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a security currently convertible into such a share` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a currently exercisable option or right to acquire such a share or such a convertible security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`share within s 126(1)` MEANS
        `it is a share carrying voting rights under all circumstances`
    OR  `it is a share carrying voting rights by reason of the occurrence of an event that has occurred and that is continuing`
    OR  `it is a security currently convertible into such a share`
    OR  `it is a currently exercisable option or right to acquire such a share or such a convertible security`

§§ `s 126(2) -- further interpretation`

-- (a) A director or officer of a body corporate that owns, controls or directs (alone or in combination)
-- shares carrying MORE THAN the prescribed percentage of the voting rights is deemed an insider of the
-- distributing corporation. The fraction is measured over all the outstanding shares of the distributing
-- corporation, not counting shares held by the body corporate as underwriter while in the course of a
-- distribution to the public: the caller states the fraction already worked out that way. Exactly the
-- prescribed percentage is not "more than".
-- src:1566 | (a) a director or an officer of a body corporate that beneficially owns, directly or indirectly, shares of a distributing corporation, or that exercises control or direction over shares of the distributing corporation, or that has a combination of any such ownership, control and direction, carrying more than the prescribed percentage of voting rights attached to all of the outstanding shares of the distributing corporation not including shares held by the body corporate as underwriter while those shares are in the course of a distribution to the public is deemed to be an insider of the distributing corporation;
@ref CBCA s 126(2)(a) (src:1566)
GIVEN `the person is a director or an officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `fraction of the voting rights carried by the shares the body corporate beneficially owns, controls or directs, not counting shares it holds as underwriter in the course of a distribution to the public` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`deemed insider within s 126(2)(a)` MEANS
        `the person is a director or an officer of the body corporate`
    AND `fraction of the voting rights carried by the shares the body corporate beneficially owns, controls or directs, not counting shares it holds as underwriter in the course of a distribution to the public` GREATER THAN `the prescribed percentage`

-- (b) A director or officer of a subsidiary is deemed an insider of the subsidiary's holding
-- distributing corporation.
-- src:1567 | (b) a director or an officer of a body corporate that is a subsidiary is deemed to be an insider of its holding distributing corporation;
@ref CBCA s 126(2)(b) (src:1567)
GIVEN `the person is a director or an officer of a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate is a subsidiary of a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`deemed insider within s 126(2)(b)` MEANS
        `the person is a director or an officer of a body corporate`
    AND `the body corporate is a subsidiary of a distributing corporation`

-- (c) A person is deemed to own beneficially the shares that a body corporate controlled (directly or
-- indirectly) by the person owns beneficially. The rule counts the shares: the person's own, plus the
-- shares of each controlled body corporate (one number per body corporate).
-- src:1568 | (c) a person is deemed to beneficially own shares that are beneficially owned by a body corporate controlled directly or indirectly by the person;
@ref CBCA s 126(2)(c) (src:1568)
GIVEN `the shares the person beneficially owns otherwise` IS A NUMBER
      `the shares beneficially owned by each body corporate the person controls directly or indirectly` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`shares deemed beneficially owned by a person within s 126(2)(c)` MEANS
    `the shares the person beneficially owns otherwise` PLUS sum `the shares beneficially owned by each body corporate the person controls directly or indirectly`

-- (d) A body corporate is deemed to own beneficially the shares that its affiliates own beneficially.
-- src:1569 | (d) a body corporate is deemed to own beneficially shares beneficially owned by its affiliates; and
@ref CBCA s 126(2)(d) (src:1569)
GIVEN `the shares the body corporate beneficially owns otherwise` IS A NUMBER
      `the shares beneficially owned by each affiliate of the body corporate` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`shares deemed beneficially owned by a body corporate within s 126(2)(d)` MEANS
    `the shares the body corporate beneficially owns otherwise` PLUS sum `the shares beneficially owned by each affiliate of the body corporate`

-- (e) An insider's acquisition or disposition of an option or right to acquire a share is deemed a
-- change in the beneficial ownership of the share to which the option or right relates.
-- src:1570 | (e) the acquisition or disposition by an insider of an option or right to acquire a share is deemed to be a change in the beneficial ownership of the share to which the option or right to acquire relates.
@ref CBCA s 126(2)(e) (src:1570)
GIVEN `the person is an insider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is an acquisition or disposition of an option or right to acquire a share` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`change in beneficial ownership deemed within s 126(2)(e)` MEANS
        `the person is an insider`
    AND `the transaction is an acquisition or disposition of an option or right to acquire a share`

§§ `s 130 -- prohibition of short sale, calls and puts`

-- (1) The relation: the insider owes everyone (the market) the abstention; the Act gives no private claim
-- here, only the offence in (4). "Knowingly" and "directly or indirectly" qualify the sale. The prohibition
-- bites if the insider does not own the security OR has not fully paid for it. The security is one of a
-- distributing corporation or of any of its affiliates.
-- src:1574 | 130 (1) An insider shall not knowingly sell, directly or indirectly, a security of a distributing corporation or any of its affiliates if the insider selling the security does not own or has not fully paid for the security to be sold.
@ref CBCA s 130(1) (src:1574)
GIVEN `the person is an insider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly sells the security, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security is a security of a distributing corporation or of any of its affiliates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person selling does not own the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person selling has not fully paid for the security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a short sale is prohibited within s 130(1)` MEANS
        `the person is an insider`
    AND `the person knowingly sells the security, directly or indirectly`
    AND `the security is a security of a distributing corporation or of any of its affiliates`
    AND (    `the person selling does not own the security`
         OR  `the person selling has not fully paid for the security`)

-- (2) "the corporation" in this subsection is read as the distributing corporation of subsection (1)
-- (fork F-130-2). A call is an option to demand delivery; a put is an option to deliver (keel: s 2(1)).
-- src:1576 | (2) An insider shall not knowingly, directly or indirectly, sell a call or buy a put in respect of a security of the corporation or any of its affiliates.
@ref CBCA s 130(2) (src:1576)
GIVEN `the person is an insider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly, directly or indirectly, sells a call` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly, directly or indirectly, buys a put` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the call or put is in respect of a security of the corporation or any of its affiliates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`selling a call or buying a put is prohibited within s 130(2)` MEANS
        `the person is an insider`
    AND (    `the person knowingly, directly or indirectly, sells a call`
         OR  `the person knowingly, directly or indirectly, buys a put`)
    AND `the call or put is in respect of a security of the corporation or any of its affiliates`

-- (3) Despite (1), an insider may sell a security they do not own if they own another security
-- convertible into it, or an option or right to acquire it, and within ten days after the sale they
-- either (a) exercise the conversion privilege, option or right and deliver the security so acquired to
-- the purchaser, or (b) transfer the convertible security, option or right to the purchaser.
-- "Within ten days after the sale": the sale day is the start and the tenth day after it is in time
-- (the keel's convention, fork F1). The exception reaches only an insider who does NOT OWN the security;
-- one who owns it but has not fully paid for it is not relieved (fork F-130-3). It does not touch (2).
-- The ten days:
-- src:1577 | Exception
-- src:1578 | (3) Despite subsection (1), an insider may sell a security they do not own if they own another security convertible into the security sold or an option or right to acquire the security sold and, within ten days after the sale, they
@ref CBCA s 130(3) (src:1577-1578)
`the ten days of s 130(3)` MEANS `Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 10, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`

-- The date on which (a) or (b) was done is NOTHING if it was not done.
-- src:1579 | (a) exercise the conversion privilege, option or right and deliver the security so acquired to the purchaser; or
-- src:1580 | (b) transfer the convertible security, option or right to the purchaser.
@ref CBCA s 130(3)(a), (b) (src:1579-1580)
GIVEN `the person selling does not own the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person owns another security convertible into the security sold, or an option or right to acquire it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the sale` IS A DATE
      `the date the person exercised the conversion privilege, option or right and delivered the security so acquired to the purchaser` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the person transferred the convertible security, option or right to the purchaser` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the exception to a short sale applies within s 130(3)` MEANS
        `the person selling does not own the security`
    AND `the person owns another security convertible into the security sold, or an option or right to acquire it`
    AND (    `done in time after the sale within s 130(3)` `the date of the sale` `the date the person exercised the conversion privilege, option or right and delivered the security so acquired to the purchaser`
         OR  `done in time after the sale within s 130(3)` `the date of the sale` `the date the person transferred the convertible security, option or right to the purchaser`)

-- A helper: an act is done within the ten days after the sale. Not done (NOTHING) is not in time.
@ref CBCA s 130(3) helper (src:1578)
GIVEN `the date of the sale` IS A DATE
      `the date the act was done` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`done in time after the sale within s 130(3)` `the date of the sale` `the date the act was done` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the act was done`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST done THEN `done within the time limit` `the ten days of s 130(3)` `the date of the sale` done

-- An insider contravenes (1) if the sale is prohibited by (1) and the exception does not apply; contravenes
-- (2) if the call or put is prohibited. (This is the condition of the offence in (4).)
@ref CBCA s 130(1), (2), (3) helper (src:1574 src:1576 src:1577-1580)
GIVEN `a short sale is prohibited within s 130(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception to a short sale applies within s 130(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `selling a call or buying a put is prohibited within s 130(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the insider contravenes s 130(1) or (2) within s 130(4)` MEANS
        (    `a short sale is prohibited within s 130(1)` AND (NOT `the exception to a short sale applies within s 130(3)`))
    OR  `selling a call or buying a put is prohibited within s 130(2)`

-- (4) The offence: an insider who contravenes (1) or (2) is guilty and liable on summary conviction to a
-- fine not exceeding the GREATER of one million dollars and three times the profit made, or to imprisonment
-- not exceeding six months, or to both. The ceiling is computed; the sentence passed is a fact about a case.
-- The crossover is a profit of 333,333.33 (three times that is one million); a loss gives a ceiling of one
-- million, because three times a negative profit is below it.
-- src:1582 | (4) An insider who contravenes subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding the greater of one million dollars and three times the profit made, or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
@ref CBCA s 130(4) (src:1582)
GIVEN `the insider contravenes s 130(1) or (2) within s 130(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the insider is guilty of an offence within s 130(4)` MEANS
    `the insider contravenes s 130(1) or (2) within s 130(4)`

@ref CBCA s 130(4) (src:1582)
GIVEN `the profit made, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV`
`the penalty ceiling within s 130(4)` MEANS
    `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV` WITH
        `maximum fine in dollars` IS IF 3 TIMES `the profit made, in dollars` GREATER THAN 1_000_000 THEN 3 TIMES `the profit made, in dollars` ELSE 1_000_000
        `maximum imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6

§§ `s 131(1) -- who is an insider, for this section`

-- Facts about one person's connection to a corporation: one record, because limbs (c), (e), (g) and (h)
-- read the same facts, and because s 131(3.1) applies limbs (b) to (i) again to a person who proposes a
-- take-over bid or a business combination, "corporation" being read as that person.
-- src:1584 | 131 (1) In this section, insider means, with respect to a corporation,
-- src:1585 | (a) the corporation;
-- src:1586 | (b) an affiliate of the corporation;
-- src:1587 | (c) a director or an officer of the corporation or of any person described in paragraph (b), (d) or (f);
-- src:1588 | (d) a person who beneficially owns, directly or indirectly, shares of the corporation or who exercises control or direction over shares of the corporation, or who has a combination of any such ownership, control and direction, carrying more than the prescribed percentage of voting rights attached to all of the outstanding shares of the corporation not including shares held by the person as underwriter while those shares are in the course of a distribution to the public;
-- src:1589 | (e) a person, other than a person described in paragraph (f), employed or retained by the corporation or by a person described in paragraph (f);
-- src:1590 | (f) a person who engages in or proposes to engage in any business or professional activity with or on behalf of the corporation;
-- src:1591 | (g) a person who received, while they were a person described in any of paragraphs (a) to (f), material confidential information concerning the corporation;
-- src:1592 | (h) a person who receives material confidential information from a person described in this subsection or in subsection (3) or (3.1), including a person described in this paragraph, and who knows or who ought reasonably to have known that the person giving the information is a person described in this subsection or in subsection (3) or (3.1), including a person described in this paragraph; and
-- src:1593 | (i) a prescribed person.
@ref CBCA s 131(1) insider (src:1584-1593)
DECLARE `Connection of a person to a corporation under s 131(1)` HAS
    `the corporation itself` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an affiliate of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a director or an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a director or an officer of a person described in paragraph (b), (d) or (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `fraction of the voting rights beneficially owned, controlled or directed, not counting shares held as underwriter in the course of a distribution to the public` IS A NUMBER
    `employed or retained by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed or retained by a person described in paragraph (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `engages in or proposes to engage in any business or professional activity with or on behalf of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `received material confidential information concerning the corporation while a person described in any of paragraphs (a) to (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `received material confidential information from a person described in subsection 131(1), (3) or (3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knows or ought reasonably to have known that the person giving the information is such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a prescribed person` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (a)
@ref CBCA s 131(1)(a) (src:1585)
GIVEN connection IS A `Connection of a person to a corporation under s 131(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`insider within s 131(1)(a)` connection MEANS
    connection's `the corporation itself`

-- (b)
@ref CBCA s 131(1)(b) (src:1586)
GIVEN connection IS A `Connection of a person to a corporation under s 131(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`insider within s 131(1)(b)` connection MEANS
    connection's `an affiliate of the corporation`

-- (c) A director or officer of the corporation, or of any person described in (b), (d) or (f). The second
-- half takes the other person's status as a fact ("a person described in paragraph (b), (d) or (f)").
@ref CBCA s 131(1)(c) (src:1587)
GIVEN connection IS A `Connection of a person to a corporation under s 131(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`insider within s 131(1)(c)` connection MEANS
        connection's `a director or an officer of the corporation`
    OR  connection's `a director or an officer of a person described in paragraph (b), (d) or (f)`

-- (d) Owns beneficially, or controls or directs, shares carrying MORE THAN the prescribed percentage of
-- the voting rights attached to all the corporation's outstanding shares, not counting shares the person
-- holds as underwriter while in the course of a distribution to the public. The fraction is worked out
-- that way by the caller.
@ref CBCA s 131(1)(d) (src:1588)
GIVEN connection IS A `Connection of a person to a corporation under s 131(1)`
      `the prescribed percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`insider within s 131(1)(d)` connection `the prescribed percentage` MEANS
    connection's `fraction of the voting rights beneficially owned, controlled or directed, not counting shares held as underwriter in the course of a distribution to the public` GREATER THAN `the prescribed percentage`

-- (e) Employed or retained by the corporation or by a person described in (f), other than a person
-- described in (f) themselves.
@ref CBCA s 131(1)(e) (src:1589)
GIVEN connection IS A `Connection of a person to a corporation under s 131(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`insider within s 131(1)(e)` connection MEANS
        (    connection's `employed or retained by the corporation`
         OR  connection's `employed or retained by a person described in paragraph (f)`)
    AND (NOT `insider within s 131(1)(f)` connection)

-- (f) Engages in, or proposes to engage in, any business or professional activity with or on behalf of
-- the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 131(1)(f) (src:1590)
GIVEN connection IS A `Connection of a person to a corporation under s 131(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`insider within s 131(1)(f)` connection MEANS
    connection's `engages in or proposes to engage in any business or professional activity with or on behalf of the corporation`

-- (g) Received material confidential information concerning the corporation while a person described
-- in any of (a) to (f). The caller states it as a fact about the person's history.
@ref CBCA s 131(1)(g) (src:1591)
GIVEN connection IS A `Connection of a person to a corporation under s 131(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`insider within s 131(1)(g)` connection MEANS
    connection's `received material confidential information concerning the corporation while a person described in any of paragraphs (a) to (f)`

-- (h) Received material confidential information from a person described in s 131(1), (3) or (3.1)
-- (including one described in this very paragraph) AND knows or ought reasonably to have known that the
-- giver is such a person. The chain of tippees is open-ended; the giver's status is taken as the fact
-- `received material confidential information from a person described ...` (fork F-131-1h).
@ref CBCA s 131(1)(h) (src:1592)
GIVEN connection IS A `Connection of a person to a corporation under s 131(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`insider within s 131(1)(h)` connection MEANS
        connection's `received material confidential information from a person described in subsection 131(1), (3) or (3.1)`
    AND connection's `knows or ought reasonably to have known that the person giving the information is such a person`

-- (i) A prescribed person (the regulations; not a source).
@ref CBCA s 131(1)(i) (src:1593)
GIVEN connection IS A `Connection of a person to a corporation under s 131(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`insider within s 131(1)(i)` connection MEANS
    connection's `a prescribed person`

-- Limbs (b) to (i) together: this is what s 131(3.1) applies to a person who proposes a take-over bid or a
-- business combination, reading "corporation" as that person.
@ref CBCA s 131(1)(b) to (i) helper (src:1586-1593)
GIVEN connection IS A `Connection of a person to a corporation under s 131(1)`
      `the prescribed percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`insider within s 131(1)(b) to (i)` connection `the prescribed percentage` MEANS
        `insider within s 131(1)(b)` connection
    OR  `insider within s 131(1)(c)` connection
    OR  `insider within s 131(1)(d)` connection `the prescribed percentage`
    OR  `insider within s 131(1)(e)` connection
    OR  `insider within s 131(1)(f)` connection
    OR  `insider within s 131(1)(g)` connection
    OR  `insider within s 131(1)(h)` connection
    OR  `insider within s 131(1)(i)` connection

-- The definition: any of (a) to (i).
@ref CBCA s 131(1) insider (src:1584-1593)
GIVEN connection IS A `Connection of a person to a corporation under s 131(1)`
      `the prescribed percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`insider within s 131(1)` connection `the prescribed percentage` MEANS
        `insider within s 131(1)(a)` connection
    OR  `insider within s 131(1)(b) to (i)` connection `the prescribed percentage`

§§ `s 131(2) -- expanded definition of security`

-- For this section a put, call, option or other right or obligation to purchase or sell a security of the
-- corporation, and a security of another entity whose market price varies materially with the market price
-- of the corporation's securities, are deemed securities of the corporation. "Material" variation is a
-- judgment of fact taken as the input.
-- src:1595 | (2) For the purposes of this section, the following are deemed to be a security of the corporation:
-- src:1596 | (a) a put, call, option or other right or obligation to purchase or sell a security of the corporation; and
-- src:1597 | (b) a security of another entity, the market price of which varies materially with the market price of the securities of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 131(2) (src:1595-1597)
GIVEN `it is a security of the corporation apart from this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a put, call, option or other right or obligation to purchase or sell a security of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a security of another entity the market price of which varies materially with the market price of the securities of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`security of the corporation within s 131(2)` MEANS
        `it is a security of the corporation apart from this subsection`
    OR  `it is a put, call, option or other right or obligation to purchase or sell a security of the corporation`
    OR  `it is a security of another entity the market price of which varies materially with the market price of the securities of the corporation`

§§ `s 131(3), (3.1) -- deemed insiders`

-- (3) A person who proposes to make a take-over bid (as defined in the regulations) for securities of the
-- corporation, or to enter into a business combination with it, is an insider "with respect to material
-- confidential information obtained from the corporation" and is an insider for the purposes of (6).
-- The rule says whether the person is such a deemed insider; the limit to information obtained from the
-- corporation is applied in `insider with respect to the information within s 131(1), (3) and (3.1)`.
-- src:1599 | (3) For the purposes of this section, a person who proposes to make a take-over bid (as defined in the regulations) for securities of a corporation, or to enter into a business combination with a corporation, is an insider of the corporation with respect to material confidential information obtained from the corporation and is an insider of the corporation for the purposes of subsection (6).
@ref CBCA s 131(3) (src:1599)
GIVEN `the person proposes to make a take-over bid, as defined in the regulations, for securities of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proposes to enter into a business combination with the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`deemed insider within s 131(3)` MEANS
        `the person proposes to make a take-over bid, as defined in the regulations, for securities of the corporation`
    OR  `the person proposes to enter into a business combination with the corporation`

-- (3.1) An insider of a person described in (3), and an affiliate or associate of such a person, is an
-- insider of the corporation. (1)(b) to (i) apply to decide whether a person is an insider of the (3)
-- person, with "corporation" read as the (3) person: the same record, about the bidder. The affiliate
-- or associate limb is a fact (the keel's `associate within s 2(1)` and the affiliate rules decide it).
-- src:1601 | (3.1) An insider of a person referred to in subsection (3), and an affiliate or associate of such a person, is an insider of the corporation referred to in that subsection. Paragraphs (1)(b) to (i) apply in determining whether a person is such an insider except that references to “corporation” in those paragraphs are to be read as references to “person described in subsection (3)”.
@ref CBCA s 131(3.1) (src:1601)
GIVEN connection IS A `Connection of a person to a corporation under s 131(1)`
      `the prescribed percentage` IS A NUMBER
      `the person is an affiliate or associate of a person described in subsection 131(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`insider within s 131(3.1)` connection `the prescribed percentage` `the person is an affiliate or associate of a person described in subsection 131(3)` MEANS
        `insider within s 131(1)(b) to (i)` connection `the prescribed percentage`
    OR  `the person is an affiliate or associate of a person described in subsection 131(3)`

-- Whether a person is an insider of the corporation for the information in question, for ss 131(4) to (7):
-- an insider by (1), or by (3.1), or by (3) only as to information obtained from the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 131(1), (3), (3.1) helper (src:1584 src:1599 src:1601)
GIVEN `the person is an insider within s 131(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a deemed insider within s 131(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information was obtained from the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an insider within s 131(3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`insider with respect to the information within s 131(1), (3) and (3.1)` MEANS
        `the person is an insider within s 131(1)`
    OR  `the person is an insider within s 131(3.1)`
    OR  (    `the person is a deemed insider within s 131(3)`
         AND `the information was obtained from the corporation`)

§§ `s 131(4), (5) -- insider trading`

-- (4) An insider who purchases or sells a security of the corporation with knowledge of confidential
-- information that, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of any
-- of the corporation's securities, is liable to compensate the seller or the purchaser for any damages
-- suffered as a result, UNLESS the insider establishes (a) a reasonable belief the information had been
-- generally disclosed, (b) that the seller or purchaser knew, or ought reasonably to have known, the
-- information, or (c) that the trade took place in the prescribed circumstances.
-- The relation: the counterparty has the claim, the insider the duty to compensate.
-- First, the trade the subsection describes:
-- src:1603 | (4) An insider who purchases or sells a security of the corporation with knowledge of confidential information that, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of any of the securities of the corporation is liable to compensate the seller of the security or the purchaser of the security, as the case may be, for any damages suffered by the seller or purchaser as a result of the purchase or sale, unless the insider establishes that
@ref CBCA s 131(4) (src:1603)
GIVEN `the person is an insider of the corporation for the information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person purchases or sells a security of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has knowledge of confidential information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of any of the securities of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`trade described in s 131(4)` MEANS
        `the person is an insider of the corporation for the information`
    AND `the person purchases or sells a security of the corporation`
    AND `the person has knowledge of confidential information`
    AND `the information, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of any of the securities of the corporation`

-- Then the claim, unless one of the three defences is established.
-- src:1604 | (a) the insider reasonably believed that the information had been generally disclosed;
-- src:1605 | (b) the information was known, or ought reasonably to have been known, by the seller or purchaser; or
-- src:1606 | (c) the purchase or sale of the security took place in the prescribed circumstances.
@ref CBCA s 131(4) (src:1604-1606)
GIVEN `the trade is described in s 131(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insider establishes that the insider reasonably believed that the information had been generally disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insider establishes that the information was known, or ought reasonably to have been known, by the seller or purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insider establishes that the purchase or sale took place in the prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`compensation is owed to the counterparty of the trade within s 131(4)` MEANS
        `the trade is described in s 131(4)`
    AND (NOT (    `the insider establishes that the insider reasonably believed that the information had been generally disclosed`
              OR  `the insider establishes that the information was known, or ought reasonably to have been known, by the seller or purchaser`
              OR  `the insider establishes that the purchase or sale took place in the prescribed circumstances`))

-- (5) The insider is accountable to the corporation for any benefit or advantage received or receivable as
-- a result of a trade described in (4), unless the insider establishes the circumstance in (4)(a) ONLY:
-- defences (b) and (c) do not apply to (5) (finding 2 in NOTES.md).
-- The relation: the corporation has the claim, the insider the duty to account.
-- src:1608 | (5) The insider is accountable to the corporation for any benefit or advantage received or receivable by the insider as a result of a purchase or sale described in subsection (4) unless the insider establishes the circumstances described in paragraph (4)(a).
@ref CBCA s 131(5) (src:1608)
GIVEN `the trade is described in s 131(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insider establishes that the insider reasonably believed that the information had been generally disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the insider is accountable to the corporation within s 131(5)` MEANS
        `the trade is described in s 131(4)`
    AND (NOT `the insider establishes that the insider reasonably believed that the information had been generally disclosed`)

§§ `s 131(6), (7) -- tipping`

-- (6) An insider of the corporation who discloses to another person confidential information about the
-- corporation that has not been generally disclosed and that, if generally known, might reasonably be
-- expected to affect materially the value of any of its securities is liable to compensate for damages any
-- person who subsequently sells securities of the corporation to, or purchases them from, a person that
-- received the information, unless the insider establishes (a) a reasonable belief that it had been generally
-- disclosed; (b) that the claimant knew, or ought reasonably to have known, the information; (c) that the
-- disclosure was necessary in the course of the insider's business, EXCEPT if the insider is a (3) or (3.1)
-- person; or (d) if the insider is a (3) or (3.1) person, that the disclosure was necessary to effect the
-- take-over bid or the business combination.
-- The relation: the claimant (who traded with a recipient) has the claim, the insider the duty to compensate.
-- First, the disclosure the subsection describes:
-- src:1610 | (6) An insider of the corporation who discloses to another person confidential information with respect to the corporation that has not been generally disclosed and that, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of any of the securities of the corporation is liable to compensate for damages any person who subsequently sells securities of the corporation to, or purchases securities of the corporation from, any person that received the information, unless the insider establishes
@ref CBCA s 131(6) (src:1610)
GIVEN `the person is an insider of the corporation for the information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person discloses confidential information about the corporation to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information has not been generally disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of any of the securities of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`disclosure described in s 131(6)` MEANS
        `the person is an insider of the corporation for the information`
    AND `the person discloses confidential information about the corporation to another person`
    AND `the information has not been generally disclosed`
    AND `the information, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of any of the securities of the corporation`

-- Then the claim. Defence (c) is open only to an insider who is NOT a (3) or (3.1) person; defence (d) only to
-- one who is.
-- src:1611 | (a) that the insider reasonably believed that the information had been generally disclosed;
-- src:1612 | (b) that the information was known, or ought reasonably to have been known, by the person who alleges to have suffered the damages;
-- src:1613 | (c) that the disclosure of the information was necessary in the course of the business of the insider, except if the insider is a person described in subsection (3) or (3.1); or
-- src:1614 | (d) if the insider is a person described in subsection (3) or (3.1), that the disclosure of the information was necessary to effect the take-over bid or the business combination, as the case may be.
@ref CBCA s 131(6) (src:1611-1614)
GIVEN `the disclosure is described in s 131(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant subsequently sold securities of the corporation to, or purchased them from, a person that received the information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insider is a person described in subsection 131(3) or (3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insider establishes that the insider reasonably believed that the information had been generally disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insider establishes that the information was known, or ought reasonably to have been known, by the person who alleges to have suffered the damages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insider establishes that the disclosure was necessary in the course of the business of the insider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insider establishes that the disclosure was necessary to effect the take-over bid or the business combination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`compensation is owed to the claimant of the disclosure within s 131(6)` MEANS
        `the disclosure is described in s 131(6)`
    AND `the claimant subsequently sold securities of the corporation to, or purchased them from, a person that received the information`
    AND (NOT (    `the insider establishes that the insider reasonably believed that the information had been generally disclosed`
              OR  `the insider establishes that the information was known, or ought reasonably to have been known, by the person who alleges to have suffered the damages`
              OR  (    (NOT `the insider is a person described in subsection 131(3) or (3.1)`)
                   AND `the insider establishes that the disclosure was necessary in the course of the business of the insider`)
              OR  (    `the insider is a person described in subsection 131(3) or (3.1)`
                   AND `the insider establishes that the disclosure was necessary to effect the take-over bid or the business combination`)))

-- (7) The insider is accountable to the corporation for any benefit or advantage received or receivable as a
-- result of a disclosure described in (6), unless the insider establishes the circumstances in (6)(a), (c) or
-- (d): defence (b) does not apply to (7). Defences (c) and (d) are open on the same terms as in (6).
-- src:1616 | (7) The insider is accountable to the corporation for any benefit or advantage received or receivable by the insider as a result of a disclosure of the information as described in subsection (6) unless the insider establishes the circumstances described in paragraph (6)(a), (c) or (d).
@ref CBCA s 131(7) (src:1616)
GIVEN `the disclosure is described in s 131(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insider is a person described in subsection 131(3) or (3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insider establishes that the insider reasonably believed that the information had been generally disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insider establishes that the disclosure was necessary in the course of the business of the insider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insider establishes that the disclosure was necessary to effect the take-over bid or the business combination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the insider is accountable to the corporation for the disclosure within s 131(7)` MEANS
        `the disclosure is described in s 131(6)`
    AND (NOT (    `the insider establishes that the insider reasonably believed that the information had been generally disclosed`
              OR  (    (NOT `the insider is a person described in subsection 131(3) or (3.1)`)
                   AND `the insider establishes that the disclosure was necessary in the course of the business of the insider`)
              OR  (    `the insider is a person described in subsection 131(3) or (3.1)`
                   AND `the insider establishes that the disclosure was necessary to effect the take-over bid or the business combination`)))

§§ `s 131(8) -- measure of damages`

-- The court may assess damages under (4) or (6) by any measure it considers relevant. But where the
-- security is a security of a distributing corporation the court MUST CONSIDER the amounts below. They are
-- a floor of what the court looks at, not an award (fork F-131-8). The average market price over the twenty
-- trading days immediately following general disclosure is a plain input: "trading days" are not in the
-- core's units.
-- src:1618 | (8) The court may assess damages under subsection (4) or (6) in accordance with any measure of damages that it considers relevant in the circumstances. However, in assessing damages in a situation involving a security of a distributing corporation, the court must consider the following:
@ref CBCA s 131(8) (src:1618)
GIVEN `the security is a security of a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court must consider the comparison with the post-disclosure price within s 131(8)` MEANS
    `the security is a security of a distributing corporation`

-- (a) The plaintiff is a purchaser: the price paid by the plaintiff for the security, less the average market
-- price over the twenty trading days immediately following general disclosure of the information.
-- src:1619 | (a) if the plaintiff is a purchaser, the price paid by the plaintiff for the security less the average market price of the security over the twenty trading days immediately following general disclosure of the information; and
@ref CBCA s 131(8)(a) (src:1619)
GIVEN `the price paid by the plaintiff for the security, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the average market price of the security over the twenty trading days immediately following general disclosure of the information, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`amount the court must consider where the plaintiff is a purchaser within s 131(8)(a)` MEANS
    `the price paid by the plaintiff for the security, in dollars` MINUS `the average market price of the security over the twenty trading days immediately following general disclosure of the information, in dollars`

-- (b) The plaintiff is a seller: the average market price over the same twenty trading days, less the price the
-- plaintiff received for the security.
-- src:1620 | (b) if the plaintiff is a seller, the average market price of the security over the twenty trading days immediately following general disclosure of the information, less the price that the plaintiff received for the security.
@ref CBCA s 131(8)(b) (src:1620)
GIVEN `the average market price of the security over the twenty trading days immediately following general disclosure of the information, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the price the plaintiff received for the security, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`amount the court must consider where the plaintiff is a seller within s 131(8)(b)` MEANS
    `the average market price of the security over the twenty trading days immediately following general disclosure of the information, in dollars` MINUS `the price the plaintiff received for the security, in dollars`

§§ `s 131(9) -- joint and several liability`

-- If more than one insider is liable under (4) or (6) with respect to the same transaction or series of
-- transactions, their liability is joint and several, or solidary: each is liable to the claimant for the whole.
-- src:1622 | (9) If more than one insider is liable under subsection (4) or (6) with respect to the same transaction or series of transactions, their liability is joint and several, or solidary.
@ref CBCA s 131(9) (src:1622)
GIVEN `the number of insiders liable under subsection 131(4) or (6) with respect to the same transaction or series of transactions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`liability is joint and several within s 131(9)` MEANS
    `the number of insiders liable under subsection 131(4) or (6) with respect to the same transaction or series of transactions` GREATER THAN 1

§§ `s 131(10) -- limitation`

-- An action to enforce a right created by (4) to (7) may be commenced only within two years after
-- discovery of the facts that gave rise to the cause of action. The discovery day is the start; the last day
-- is two years later (the keel's convention, fork F1).
-- src:1624 | (10) An action to enforce a right created by subsections (4) to (7) may be commenced only within two years after discovery of the facts that gave rise to the cause of action.
@ref CBCA s 131(10) (src:1624)
`the two years of s 131(10)` MEANS `Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 2, `unit of time` IS `calendar years`

@ref CBCA s 131(10) (src:1624)
GIVEN `the date the facts that gave rise to the cause of action were discovered` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to commence an action within s 131(10)` MEANS
    `the last day of` `the two years of s 131(10)` `counted from` `the date the facts that gave rise to the cause of action were discovered`

@ref CBCA s 131(10) (src:1624)
GIVEN `the date the facts that gave rise to the cause of action were discovered` IS A DATE
      `the date the action is commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an action may be commenced within s 131(10)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` `the two years of s 131(10)` `the date the facts that gave rise to the cause of action were discovered` `the date the action is commenced`
